<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/903458730%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Başbük";
    rdfs:comment "This modern village in Turkey's Şanlıurfa province is the site of a subterranean complex discovered in 2017 and only partially excavated. The excavated portion of the complex can be dated to the Neo-ssyrian period, thanks to the presence of an unfinished, rock wall panel depicting a divine procession with some divine figures labeled in Aramaic.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/903458730> .

