<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/91288718%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Tholos of Athens";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/720198157%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/807514119%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The so-called \"Tholos\" located on the west side of the Athenian Agora was a circular civic building that took the place of archaic-period buildings associated with the Peisistratid tyrants. The Classical tholos served as a civic dining hall for the prytany council.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/91288718> .

