<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912909%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Nina";
    rdfs:comment "Tell Zurghul is an archaeological site in Iraq covering approximately 70 ha. The site includes two settlement mounds. The ancient site was located on a canal leading away from Lagash, some 10 km to the southeast. The ancient name of this place was Niĝin (or Nina or Ninua), and Nanshe (Nanše) was the titular divinity.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912909> .

