<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/922716%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Sar Mashhad";
    rdfs:comment "Sar Mashhad, located in the Dadin Rural District, Jereh and Baladeh District, Kazerun County, Fars Province, Iran, is the site of a Sasanian rock relief of a lion hunt, along with accompanying inscriptions. The monument dates to the reign of the king Bahram II (r. 274–293 CE).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/922716> .

