    rdfs:comment "The so-called \"Arco Etrusco\" is one of the gates of ancient Perusia. The gate dates originally from the third century B.C. when it was one of seven gates in the Etruscan wall. In 40 B.C. it was refashioned under Augustus.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/923690483> .

