<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/924184480%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Mound at Banāt al-Hassan (Adams 131)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/3601983%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/690025800%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Part of a group of mounds in central Mesopotamia, this settlement (number 131 in Adams 1972) contained remains dated to the Early Dynastic I-Old Babylonian periods (chiefly Ur III-Larsa). The site also contains a number of burials from the Parthian period, fragments of Sasanian pottery, and the remains of an Early Islamic structure.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/924184480> .

