<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/928072777%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Benches on Kolonos Agoraios";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/146086514%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/807514119%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A set of poros benches built on the east slope of the Kolonos Agoraios at the edge of the Athenian Agora in the fifth century BC, which seated 400-500 people and perhaps served as a meeting place for a council or court. They were truncated and rendered inaccessible by further construction in the fourth century BC.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/928072777> .

