<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/929709014%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Kavuncu";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/214160492%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Kavuncu is a modern settlement situated near Van in the southeast of Turkey. Here a cylindrical stone (probably a column base) with an inscription of the Urartian king Minua, son of Išpuini (9/8th century BCE) was found (CTU I A 5-53 B).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/929709014> .

