<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/933523997%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Amnya River";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/505085395%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Amnya River (Russian: Амня) is a left tributary of the Kasym in the Khanty-Mansi Autonomous Okrug/Ugra of Western Siberia. It flows predominantly northward through the West Siberian Plain and joins the Kasym about 15 km east of Beloyarsky. The river flows for some 374 km from its source to the point of confluence and drains an area of 7210 km².";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/933523997> .

