    rdfs:comment "Hazine Piri Kapısı is the Turkish name for a rock niche bearing an inscription of the Urartian king Išpuini, son of Sarduri I (9th century BCE). It is situated on an isolated rock near modern Elmalı (Zivistan) and Edremit.";
