    rdfs:label "Isola Conversina";
    rdfs:comment "The ruined tower of Isola Conversina, also known as Torre della Stroppa, is located on a tuff ridge with steep margins that has likely been inhabited since the Bronze Age. This hill is located along the line of the Via Amerina. The present ruined castle dates to the Medieval period.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/960644233> .

