    rdfs:comment "Thatta was the capital of three successive dynasties and later ruled by the Mughal emperors of Delhi. The expansive necropolis is thought to have grown around the fourteenth-century shrine of Muhammad Hussain Abro.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/961231336> .

