<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/986274170%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Horologium Augusti";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422863%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/816091000%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Horologium Augusti or Solarium Augusti was an ancient monument of the Campus Martius built during the reign of Augustus. In theory, it functioned as a giant solar marker. An obelisk relocated to Rome from Heliopolis served as the gnomon. The obelisk today stands in the Piazza di Monte Citorio.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/986274170> .

