    rdfs:label "Valløby";
    rdfs:comment "An ancient \"princely\" grave was discovered in the 19th century at the village of Valløby in Denmark. Among the grave goods were some Roman imports. It is not known if the tomb, which was reportedly marked by a circular stone structure, was singular or part of a larger cemetery.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/99054> .

