<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/99304503945%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Alpes Graiae (province)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/167637%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A small Alpine province of the Roman Empire organized around the Little St Bernard Pass, roughly corresponding to the eastern portion of the modern-day French department of Savoie. Augustus annexed the territory in 15 BCE; under Diocletian, the periodically joint administration of the province together with Alpes Poeninae was made permanent, forming the province of Alpes Poeninae et Graiae.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/99304503945> .

