        "MANTO 11320294: Augustan Villa (Boscotrecase)",
        "Molacek et al. 2020 ",
        "NSc 19 (1922) 478",
        "PompeiiinPictures Boscotrecase, Villa Agrippa Postumus or Imperial Villa.",
        "The Augustan Villa at Boscotrecase (2004) ",
        "Wikidata Villa of Agrippa Postumus (Q121922430)",
        "Wikipedia (English) Villa of Agrippa Postumus",
        "von Blanckenhagen 1962 ",
        "von Blanckenhagen 1990 ";
    dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/acampbell>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/ghawes>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/rssmith>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "The Villa of Agrippa Postumus was discovered at Boscotrecase in 1903 on land owned by Cavaliere Ernesto Santini. Works for the Circumvesuviana railroad line brought the site to light. Excavations supervised by Matteo Della Corte were carried out from 1903 to 1905. In 1906, however, a new eruption of Mount Vesuvius reburied the site. Della Corte published a plan of the excavated portion of the villa in the Notizie degli scavi di antichità.";
