        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "The so-called \"Tholos\" located on the west side of the Athenian Agora was a circular civic building that took the place of archaic-period buildings associated with the Peisistratid tyrants. The Classical tholos served as a civic dining hall for the prytany council.";
