    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/cjohansson>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/rrattenborg>;
    dcterms:description "Part of a group of mounds in central Mesopotamia, this settlement (number 131 in Adams 1972) contained remains dated to the Early Dynastic I-Old Babylonian periods (chiefly Ur III-Larsa). The site also contains a number of burials from the Parthian period, fragments of Sasanian pottery, and the remains of an Early Islamic structure.";
