    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "AAA 15.78 El Guerria",
        "AAA 15.91 Lecourbe (Ouled Agla), second column, first full paragraph and following",
        "BAtlDir page 489 sub \"Unidentified Point Symbols\" see \"B4 settlements\"",
        "BAtlas 31 B4",
        "EDCS 25001059 =  CIL 8.8813",
        "EDCS 25001060 = CIL 8.8814 = ILS 5960",
        "EDCS 26100141 = CIL 8.10430";
    dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/rtalbert>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/56622759>;
    dcterms:description "Remains of superimposed Arab and Roman settlements recorded by Gsell (AAA, whence BAtlas) on and around a hill about three kilometers to the southwest of the village of \"Medjana\" at \"El Guerria\" on the \"Oued Lechbour\". The location should lie within a kilometer of the BAtlas coordinates: a point near modern Guerria and the modern road from Guerria to Meğana in the Algerian wilaya of Bordj Bou Arreridj. A nineteenth century identification of El-Guerria with attested ancient Equizito was soundly rejected by Gsell (AAA 15.91), but it is still reflected in some modern epigraphic databases.";
    dcterms:modified "2025-05-29T21:44:32-04:00";
    dcterms:title "El-Guerria";
