    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/17244949>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "In the introductory essay for Map 41 of the Barrington Atlas published in the Map-by-Map Directory, Vico Pancellorum is mentioned as a toponym with likely ancient origins, but absent is any specific evidence to that effect. Vico Pancellorum is a small Tuscan village located in the Province of Lucca. It is situated at 630 meters above sea level at the foot of Balzo Nero.";
