    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/bchristiansen2>;
    dcterms:description "The Aşağı Anzaf Fortress (\"Lower Anzaf Fortress\") is situated in the Van region in southeast Turkey. It was built by the Urartian King Išpuini (9th / 8th century BCE) who reports about his building activity in several building inscriptions (see especially the building inscription on the fortification wall (CTU A 2-6). Another fortress at Anzaf, namely Yukarı Anzaf (Upper Anzaf) was built by Išpuini's son Minua (9th / 8th century BCE).";
    dcterms:modified "2025-11-25T12:47:30-04:00";
    dcterms:subject "ANE",
        "Urartean",
        "Urartian",
