<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/981527%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Iudaea (province)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/678369%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/687927%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/687934%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/930907033%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/991396%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Roman province of Iudaea, incorporating the historical regions of Judea, Samaria, and Idumaea, was established in 6 CE, when the former tetrarchy of Herod Archelaus came under direct Roman administration. Following the Bar Kokhba War (132-135), Hadrian changed the province's name to Palaestina, and in the mid- to late 4th century CE the area was divided into three provinces (Palaestina Prima, Secunda, and Tertia or Salutaris).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/981527> .

