<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912835%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Dez/Hithite/Hudhud/Koprates? (river)";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/903015%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912829%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912879%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "This river, known by various names in antiquity, was an upstream tributary (via the Karun river) of the final stage of ancient Tigris/Pastigiris, ultimately debouching into the Persian Gulf. Today its waters still join the Karun. The modern course of the Dez lies within the modern country of Iran.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/912835> .

